==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|la|en}} {{lena}}, the head.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|capita}}

# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} The [[head]].
# {{context|anatomy|lang=en}} A [[knob]]-like [[protuberance]] or [[capitulum]].
# The [[top]] or [[superior]] part of a thing.
# {{context|UK|lang=en}} The [[council]] or ruling body of the University of [[Cambridge]] prior to the constitution of 1856.
#* Lamb
#*: Your '''caputs''' and heads of colleges.

====Related terms====
* [[caput mortuum]]

{{Webster 1913}}

